            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Are u looking for a way to read the fw version for both the sources when booted from any of them?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kimi Chen",
                        "email": "kimi.zy.chen@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "zuyan-kimi"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes. My goal is to avoid entering Program Mode to read the version, and instead directly read the currently active version.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/blob/bca506e6ba78c50ea91a45e727d9d776c6885dd4/cpld/lattice/lattice_base_cpld.cpp#L494\n\nThe original code hardcoded the target as CFG0, so I was looking into building a configurable target selection. However, I noticed that this commit has already addressed it by passing an empty string as the target in getVersion to read the currently active version instead.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/commit/37e023c278bec775578d9eb5fa9f3c661a948686"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kimi Chen",
                        "email": "kimi.zy.chen@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "zuyan-kimi"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry for the naive question \u2014 do you happen to know the historical reason why reading the version originally required entering Program Mode?\n\nAlso, would it be worth continuing to add the target property to the Entity Manager configuration to allow more flexible configuration?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/meson.build",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't understand why this is a compile option.  It seems like it should be a configuration / compatible / EM option."
                }
            ],
